+## Self-review
+
+1. **Placeholders** — none; every fence holds real code or real prose, no `TBD`.
+2. **Internal consistency** — the `past end` detail string is written once, in
+   `pastEnd`, and both call sites (link and backtick) use it, so the message a
+   test asserts on is the same message either path produces.
+3. **Scope** — one task, one file group, one test cycle. Not a decomposition
+   candidate.
+4. **Ambiguity** — "past the end" is exact: `from > total || to > total`
+   against `lineCount`'s count of real lines (trailing newline not counted,
+   per `docs-check.js`'s own `linesOf`).
+5. **Against the project** — checked against `.fankeel/map.md` above; no
+   conflict, and the design this argues from is correctly filed as `plan`
+   (design-intent, not yet built).
